  body: |
    # Self-employed earner in the ESA source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source describes self-employment as gainful employment in Great Britain outside employed-earner employment, while allowing a person to have separate employed work.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 50007 and 50016 distinguish limited-company directors as office holders. The separate claimant/partner effects in ESA(Cont) and ESA(IR) remain explicit; neither a business label nor tax treatment alone determines the outcome.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 50007, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/61976ff0d3bf7f055fce727f/dmgch50.pdf#page=2)
    - [DMG 50016, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/61976ff0d3bf7f055fce727f/dmgch50.pdf#page=5)
    - [DMG 50004, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/61976ff0d3bf7f055fce727f/dmgch50.pdf#page=2)
    - [DMG 50005, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/61976ff0d3bf7f055fce727f/dmgch50.pdf#page=2)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

