  - target: term/esa-employed-earner
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source distinguishes the statuses while allowing separate work in both and identifies limited-company directors as employed earners.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch50/0002
      quote: "50007 A S/E earner is a person who is gainfully employed\n\n\n1. in GB and\n\n\n2. in employment that is not employed earners employment1.\n\n\nNote: A person may also be employed as an employed earner. This does not stop the person being S/E.\n\n\n                                                                1 ESA Regs, reg 2(1); SS CB Act 92, s 2(1)(b)"
      locator: DMG 50007
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch50/0005
      quote: "50016 A limited company, of whatever size, is separate from its employees, officers and shareholders 1.\nThis means that the profits of the company do not belong to the directors. A director of a limited\n\ncompany is an office holder in the company2 and is an employed earner (see DMG Chapter 49).\n\n\n                                                             1 R(SB) 57/83; 2 McMillan v Guest 1942, AC 561\n\n\n\nEarnings of self-employed earners"
      locator: DMG 50016
